<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch November producer prices rise 2.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch November producer prices rise 2.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch producer price index (PPI) for manufactured goods fell a provisional 0.7 percent in November from October, giving a 2.6 percent rise year-on-year, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p> DUTCH PRODUCER PRICES	  Nov 96     Oct 96     Nov 95</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		102.6	103.3	100.0</p>
<p> Month-on-month pct change     -0.7	  0.5	 -0.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year pct change	  2.6	  3.2	  0.2</p>
<p> Subindex domestic prices     106.2	106.7	104.1</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		   2.0	  2.5	  1.3</p>
<p> Subindex export prices	  99.8	100.6	 96.8</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		   3.1	  3.7	 -0.7</p>
<p>-- Andrew Kelly, Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 570 8500</p>
</text>
